  "description": "Description of proposed works: Felling of one mature Lime tree (T1) - Tilia platyphyllos, approximately 20m in height with 10m crown spread, located at the south corner of Rosendene Nursing Home (overhanging Dalebury Road and neighbouring property). The tree has outgrown its confined raised bed location and is causing structural damage and subsidence to surrounding walls. A heavy ivy infestation covers most of the trunk and crown, weakening the tree???s structure and increasing risk of branch failure. The rooting environment is inadequate for a tree of this size, raising long-term stability and safety concerns. Removal is requested on grounds of safety, structural damage, and amenity concerns expressed by both the nursing home management and local residents.",
